name: two-arg-if-gaps-when-false
why: if(c, x) with no else plots x only while c holds; a false condition is NO point, never a fabricated branch. price>3 admits only t2 (5>3). t1(1>3) and t3(2>3) are false → gaps.
expr: if(nodeA.price > 3, nodeA.price)
keys: nodeA.price
resolve: LOCF
--- LOG ---
---
#00:00:01.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 1
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 1.0}
---
#00:00:02.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 2
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 5.0}
---
#00:00:03.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 3
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 2.0}
--- EXPECT ---
2 => 5.0
